{"step_index":5369,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-23T16:25:07Z","thinking":"The audit reveals an incorrect match due to shared brand names, despite differing product categories: shampoo versus antiseptic. Another mismatch involves a possible insulin product.\n\n\nThe analysis now extends to mismatches where the core product or dosage differs despite a shared brand name, such as insulin type, or differing strengths of augmentin. Differences like formulation (cream vs. suppository) and product type (e.g., milk stage) are also being flagged as discrepancies. Other incorrect matches are arising from drug name similarities, like Eucarbon versus Neo-carbon.\n\n\nThe root cause of incorrect matches appears to be failing to distinguish between brand families versus specific product names, along with inadequate handling of varying strengths and formulations. This highlights the limitations of purely string-based matching, leading to discrepancies when only brand names are similar. This reinforces the need for more sophisticated logic. The `coordinator` in the previous procedure's success resulted from a high-confidence auto-match rule, coupled with the ability to dispatch complex cases to a more nuanced clinical evaluation.\n\n\nPROC-007's primary failure stems from two issues: the incorrect handling of \"no_match\" results, sending potentially valid matches to \"not found,\" and overly conservative LLM behavior that discards acceptable matches based on packaging differences. A three-level architecture is needed, starting with fast candidate discovery, followed by LLM-driven refinement, and culminating in clinical review for edge cases. The architecture must prioritize reviewing high-confidence brand matches before discarding them.\n\n\nA clear \"not found\" determination arises when no candidates are identified in any warehouse. High-confidence auto-matches occur with exact text matches, high TF-IDF scores, or brand matches considering packaging variations. Remaining candidates undergo LLM evaluation, followed by deterministic post-LLM validation when the LLM suggests a match, or a review if the LLM suggests a \"no_match\" or omits a decision.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"write_to_file","args":{"ArtifactMetadata":{"RequestFeedback":false,"Summary":"Test the exact 3-level coordinator logic","UserFacing":false},"CodeContent":"import sys\nsys.path.insert(0, \".\")\nimport json\nimport re\nfrom pathlib import Path\nfrom rapidfuzz import fuzz\n\nfrom src.extract.excel_reader import read_excel, extract_item_names\nfrom src.extract.file_handler import read_input_files\nfrom src.fast_match.search import (\n    FastCandidateFinder,\n    extract_brand_tokens,\n    extract_form_group,\n    normalize_text,\n    FORM_GROUPS\n)\nfrom src.config import load_config\n\n# Helper to normalize arabic numbers\ndef norm_num(s: str) -> str:\n    s = str(s)\n    for e, w in zip('٠١٢٣٤٥٦٧٨٩', '0123456789'):\n        s = s.replace(e, w)\n    return s\n\ndef get_strength_pattern(text: str) -> str | None:\n    text = norm_num(text.lower())\n    m = re.search(r'(\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?)\\s*(?:مجم|مج|جم|جرام|gm|mg|mcg|مكجم)', text)\n    if m:\n        return m.group(1)\n    if 'ربع' in text or '25.' in text:\n        return '0.25'\n    if 'نص' in text or 'نصف' in text or '.5' in text or '0.5' in text:\n        return '0.5'\n    return None\n\ndef has_co(text: str) -> bool:\n    t = text.lower()\n    return bool(re.search(r'(?:^|[^\\w])(كو|بلس|بلاس|كومب|co|plus|comp)(?:[^\\w]|$)|كواقراص|كوأقراص|بلساقراص|بلسكبسول', t))\n\ndef are_forms_compatible(form1: str | None, form2: str | None) -> bool:\n    if not form1 or not form2:\n        return True\n    if form1 == form2:\n        return True\n    compat = {\n        ('tablet', 'capsule'), ('capsule', 'tablet'),\n        ('cream', 'ointment'), ('ointment', 'cream'),\n        ('cream', 'gel'), ('gel', 'cream'),\n        ('injection', 'ampoule'), ('ampoule', 'injection'),\n    }\n    return (form1, form2) in compat\n\n# Brand Family Stopwords that need secondary tokens to match\nBRAND_FAMILIES = {'بيتادين', 'هيرو', 'انسولين', 'ليمتلس', 'سيتال', 'لبن'}\n\ndef is_safe_auto_match(req: str, cand: str) -> tuple[bool, str]:\n    brand_r = extract_brand_tokens(req)\n    brand_c = extract_brand_tokens(cand)\n    if not brand_r or not brand_c:\n        return False, \"no_brand\"\n        \n    words_r = brand_r.split()\n    words_c = brand_c.split()\n    \n    # If brand belongs to a wide family, brand must match beyond the first word\n    first_r = words_r[0]\n    first_c = words_c[0]\n    if first_r in BRAND_FAMILIES or first_c in BRAND_FAMILIES:\n        # Full brand string must match well\n        if fuzz.ratio(brand_r, brand_c) < 85:\n            return False, \"brand_family_ambiguity\"\n            \n    b_sim = fuzz.ratio(brand_r, brand_c)\n    if words_r and words_c and (words_r[0] == words_c[0] or fuzz.ratio(words_r[0], words_c[0]) >= 85):\n        if len(words_r) == 1 and len(words_c) == 1:\n            b_sim = max(b_sim, 90)\n            \n    if b_sim < 85:\n        return False, \"low_brand_sim\"\n        \n    form_r = extract_form_group(req)\n    form_c = extract_form_group(cand)\n    if not are_forms_compatible(form_r, form_c):\n        return False, \"form_conflict\"\n        \n    is_req_syrup = bool(re.search(r'\\b(شراب|شرب|معلق)\\b', req))\n    is_cand_syrup = bool(re.search(r'\\b(شراب|شرب|معلق)\\b', cand))\n    norm_c = norm_num(cand)\n    norm_r = norm_num(req)\n    has_c_solid_mg = bool(re.search(r'\\b(100|125|200|250|300|400|500|600|800|1000)\\s*(?:مجم|مج|mg)\\b', norm_c)) and not re.search(r'\\b(مل|ملل|ml|/5|5مل)\\b', norm_c)\n    has_r_solid_mg = bool(re.search(r'\\b(100|125|200|250|300|400|500|600|800|1000)\\s*(?:مجم|مج|mg)\\b', norm_r)) and not re.search(r'\\b(مل|ملل|ml|/5|5مل)\\b', norm_r)\n    if (is_req_syrup and not is_cand_syrup and has_c_solid_mg) or (is_cand_syrup and not is_req_syrup and has_r_solid_mg):\n        return False, \"syrup_solid_conflict\"\n        \n    if has_co(req) != has_co(cand):\n        return False, \"co_mismatch\"\n        \n    str_r = get_strength_pattern(req)\n    str_c = get_strength_pattern(cand)\n    if str_r and str_c:\n        try:\n            if float(str_r) != float(str_c):\n                return False, f\"strength_mismatch_{str_r}_vs_{str_c}\"\n        except:\n            if str_r != str_c:\n                return False, f\"strength_mismatch_{str_r}_vs_{str_c}\"\n                \n    slash_r = re.search(r'(?:^|[^\\d/])(\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?\\/\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?)(?:[^\\d/]|$)', req)\n    slash_c = re.search(r'(?:^|[^\\d/])(\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?\\/\\d+(?:\\.\\d+)?)(?:[^\\d/]|$)', cand)\n    if (slash_r and not slash_c) or (slash_c and not slash_r):\n        return False, \"slash_strength_mismatch\"\n    if slash_r and slash_c and slash_r.group(1) != slash_c.group(1):\n        return False, \"slash_strength_mismatch\"\n        \n    return True, \"auto_matched\"\n\nprint(\"Safety Auto-Match function defined successfully.\")\n","Description":"Safe auto match logic with brand family protection","Overwrite":true,"TargetFile":"C:\\Users\\kakak\\.gemini\\antigravity\\brain\\916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a\\scratch\\test_safe_auto.py","toolAction":"Writing safe auto match test","toolSummary":"Define safe auto match with brand family protection"}}]}
